      <activity id="7a5460cf-5929-5e76-a6e9-c19b6336bc3f" activityNameId="2c9739d4-3e59-5d90-bc4f-f927db881425" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Steel board, 10 mm, powder coated, cardboard filled, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Steel board, 10 mm, powder coated, cardboard filled, at plant
na;
UUID: 25a95431-5283-3439-bdba-b131e5c756fd
This data set includes the materials and resources needed for producing steel kitchen front panels per m2. The panel has a mounting plate of corrugated cardboard which is coverd with the steel sheets and pressed. The cardboard core is about 1 cm wide and shows an average width for shelfs, sidewalls and tops and bottoms. Tops and bottoms have usually a width of 16 mm while side walls and shelfs have a width of 8 mm. It is assumed that the pressing consumes as much electricity as the steel processing of Franke (kitchen worktop production). Transport is estimated according to the ecoinvent standard distances for Switzerland.; Geography: Data valid for Switzerland
Location:  Data valid for Switzerland
Technology: Average disposal
Time period: &lt;null&gt;
Production volume: na
Sampling: unknown 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_25a95431-5283-3439-bdba-b131e5c756fd.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
